[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H10TG-58
TITLE: Treatment Console - Radiation Emission Control - Prepare process - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
Verify the user interface layout of the application accurately reflects the system's status and button labels during the treatment preparation process.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
Load a plan for treatment in the Heracles Internal unit.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Log in to the External application. 

2. Navigate to the treatment view. 

3. Press the Prepare button to prepare the treatment.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1 - The interface should display the following states: 

System status: COLD 

Button Label: Prepare 

3 - The interface should display the following states: 

System status: WARMUP 

Button's label: Warming up ( with progress bar) 

then System status: HVSetup ( On Loading) 

Upon completion of the preparation process: 

System status: READY
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10TG-43
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H10TG-121
TITLE: Quality Assurance - Daily Warmup
STATEMENT: >>>
Verify the daily fast-warmup and conditioning controls use the deployed targets and report
a safety rejection without recording a completed procedure.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. The system is operational and can be returned to COLD state
2. Heater-current command telemetry and warmup history are available for observation
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Log in to the External application and navigate to Startup Cycle in Quality Assurance
2. In COLD state, engage either e-stop and attempt fast warmup
3. Release both e-stops, start fast warmup, and observe the commanded heater-current target
   and warmup history when the procedure completes
4. Return to COLD, start conditioning, and observe the commanded target and warmup history
   when the procedure completes
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. The rejected fast-warmup attempt displays an error that the current state is not
   permitted and directs the operator to verify both e-stops; no completed record is added
2. With both e-stops released, fast warmup commands its configured target and completion
   adds a record to warmup history.
3. Conditioning commands its configured target and completion adds a record to warmup history.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10TG-1
  ROLE: Verifies
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10TG-29
  ROLE: Verifies
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10TG-30
  ROLE: Verifies

