[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H10TG-46
TITLE: Treatment Console - Radiation Emission Control - Beam On process - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
This test case verifies the functionality and status transitions of the Heracles External GUI during a treatment plan execution. To ensure that the system responds correctly to user interactions.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
Load a plan for treatment in the Heracles Internal unit.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Log in to the External application. 

2. Navigate to the treatment view. 

3. Press the Prepare button to prepare the treatment. 

4. Press the Beam-On button to trigger emission delivery.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
4 - The button label should transition to "Launching", and subsequently to "Beaming on" with a progress bar. 

System status at the top of the screen should be "Emission". 

Upon completion, a pop-up message should be displayed to confirm successful delivery. 

Upon approving the pop-up, the system status should change to "Termination" and the Energy level should go down to 0. 

6 - The button label should revert to "Beam On", and the system status should update to "Primed".
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10TG-9
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H10TG-136
TITLE: Quality Assurance - QC Measurement Acquisition and Diagnostics
STATEMENT: >>>
Verify that the QC path acquires detector measurements through main control, records the returned intensities, exposes detector diagnostic telemetry, and reports connection or acquisition failures.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. Run the External application with the GCB, main-control board, head, and QC detector connected.
2. Provide an approved QC detector signal source with distinguishable channel values and the ability to control detector connectivity.
3. Connect a UCSI diagnostic client that can subscribe to and record system telemetry.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Log in to the External application and start recording system telemetry with the UCSI diagnostic client.

2. In the diagnostic client, observe both QC instantaneous readings, both QC accumulations, and
   both ADC connection states.

3. Navigate to the Beam QA Checks tab in the Quality Assurance view.

4. Select Energy 50/70/100 in the Energy drop-down and select exactly one emission in the Target list.

5. Press Prepare.

6. Press Beam On and observe the QC command trace until the selected emission completes.

7. Toggle to report view and compare the acquired channel 0 and channel 1 accumulation values.

8. Stop the diagnostic recording and inspect the recorded QC readings, accumulations, and ADC
connection states.

9. Disconnect the QC detector, select one emission again, and press Prepare.

10. Reconnect the detector, prepare the emission, arrange for QC start rejection and then for a
pending stop response beyond two seconds, and press Beam On for each case.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1 - UCSI records live QC diagnostic telemetry from the connected system.

2 - Both channel readings and accumulations are identified in counts, and both ADC connection
states reflect the connected detector hardware.

5 - Prepare succeeds only after the detector responds to the QC-board connection check through
main control.

6 - The trace sends ``[Start, 0]`` before Beam On and receives Armed before radiation is requested.
After the emission, ``[Stop, 0]`` responses are polled within one shared two-second deadline until
Complete. The five unsigned response words are channel 0 sum, channel 1 sum, channel 0 count,
channel 1 count, and numeric session status.

7 - The report contains exactly the selected Target for the selected Applicator and Energy level,
with exactly two measured accumulation rows and no rows for unselected Targets.

8 - UCSI records both live accumulation fields in schema version 2; replaying a version 1 recording
represents the absent accumulation fields as null rather than rejecting the file.

9 - Prepare returns the application to StandBy and displays a preparation error; no emission can
start while the detector is unavailable.

10 - Start rejection prevents Beam On and triggers one best-effort Stop. A stop deadline expiry
stops emission, displays an acquisition error, and creates no QC result.
<<<
