[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H10TG-135
TITLE: Quality Assurance - Perform Quality Checks - Deviation
STATEMENT: >>>
This test case verifies QC deviation reporting and every QC acceptance decision used to gate
treatment preparation.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. Store two referenced QC samples for one collimator and energy configuration, with the newer
   reference containing known nonzero diode values and unused zero-valued channels.
2. Make the latest reference more than 24 hours old.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Log in to Heracles External and open Beam QA Checks.
2. Select the same collimator, energy, and QA emission as the stored references.
3. Prepare and emit a current QC sample within 24 hours of the test.
4. Open the report view, select the configuration, inspect the reference and latest results,
   switch to Deviation, and independently calculate each displayed deviation.
5. Exercise samples just inside and just outside positive and negative 3 percent deviation.
6. Exercise matching zero values, a nonzero value against a zero reference, a missing QA
   emission, and a mismatched diode-value count.
7. Exercise a configuration with no samples, one whose latest sample is older than 24 hours,
   and a current unapproved sample with no reference.
8. Mark the current sample approved and repeat the acceptance evaluation without a reference.
9. Run the QC treatment acceptance service tests.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Reporting and acceptance use the newest reference and the newest current sample for the
   selected configuration.
2. Displayed deviations match the independent calculations.
3. A sample passes only when every available diode value has an absolute deviation of less
   than 3 percent; deviation outside the limit in either direction fails the sample.
4. Matching zero values have zero deviation. A nonzero value against a zero reference, missing
   or null data, or a mismatched QA-emission or diode-value shape fails acceptance.
5. No sample or a latest sample older than 24 hours returns ``Missing``; a current unapproved
   sample without a reference returns ``NoReference``.
6. A current sample with persisted approval returns ``Accepted`` without a reference.
7. The automated tests produce the same status for every boundary and data-shape case.
<<<
