[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H10TG-61
TITLE: Radiation Emission Control - Record partial treatment - (After Two stoppings) - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
Verifying the layout for recording partial treatment, to ensure that the UI correctly displays the details of a partially completed treatment session after the emission is stopped prematurely twice.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
Create treatment field with duration of 12 Seconds and Load a plan for treatment in the Heracles Internal unit.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Launch Heracles SW External. (The external unit should be located outside the treatment room).

2. Click the Prepare button.

3. Click the Beam On button.

4. After 5 seconds (check elapsed time), Click the Stop button (during the beaming process).

5. Repeat steps 3 and 4 (Click the Beam On button, and after 2 seconds, click the Stop button).
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1 - The interface should display: System status: COLD, Button Label: Prepare

2 - The interface should display: System status: WARMUP, then PRIMED, then READY

3 - The button label should transition to "Launching", and subsequently to "Beaming on" with a progress bar.

4 - User shall receive an indicator or pop-up message indicating that the beaming has stopped. System status shall change to: READY.

5 - After stopping the emission at 5 seconds, restarting it, and then stopping it again after 2 seconds (out of total of 12 seconds), the stopped treatment field should appear in the treatment field view with Duration: 12, Remaining[sec]: 5. The remaining time should be specified with a resolution of 0.01 minutes (600msec) and marked as partial in the database.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10TG-22
  ROLE: Verifies
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10TG-13
  ROLE: Verifies

