[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H10TG-297
TITLE: Device Information Version and Telemetry Selection
STATEMENT: >>>
Verify that System Information displays the release version reported by main control and
that telemetry-layout selection depends on the reported firmware mode rather than the
release version text.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. A GCB protocol fixture can provide valid 19-word device-information and telemetry packets.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Start the external application with the fixture reporting a supported firmware mode and
   a known release version string.
2. Open System Information and record the main control board version.
3. Send valid telemetry and observe the Treatment view.
4. Change only the device-information release version string, then repeat the telemetry.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. The device-information packet is accepted.
2. System Information displays the exact reported release version string.
3. The telemetry layout for the reported mode is selected and telemetry is displayed.
4. Telemetry remains accepted under the same mode after only the release version changes.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10TG-286
  ROLE: Verifies
